problems.problem:
We are given an $n\times n$ board. The rows are labelled with the numbers $1$ to $n$ downwards and the columns with the numbers $1$ to $n$ from left to right. In each field we write the number $x^2+y^2$, where $(x,y)$ are its coordinates. We are given a figure and can initially place it on any field. In every step we can move the figure from one field to another if the other field has not already been visited and if at least one of the following conditions is satisfied:
• the numbers in those $2$ fields give the same remainder when divided by $n$;
• those fields are symmetric with respect to the centre of the board.
Can all the fields be visited in the case
a) $n=4$;
b) $n=5$?

A positive integer $k\ge 3$ is called fibby if there exist a positive integer $n$ and positive integers $d_1<d_2<\ldots<d_k$ with the following properties:
• $d_{j+2}=d_{j+1}+d_j$ for every $j$ satisfying $1\le j\le k-2$;
• $d_1, d_2, \ldots, d_k$ are divisors of $n$;
• any other divisor of $n$ is either less than $d_1$ or greater than $d_k$.
Find all fibby numbers.
